~ / g~motion / gu / gU :: Toggle / change case using a motion
qa ... q / @a / @@ :: Record macro a / replay macro a / repeat last macro
:w / :w filename :: Save / save as
:q / :wq / :q! :: Quit / save and quit / discard buffer edits and quit
:wa / :qa / :wqa :: Save all / quit all / save all and quit
:e filename :: Open or create a file
:enew :: Open empty buffer
:set paste / :set nopaste :: Toggle paste mode if terminal paste needs it
Ctrl+R + (Insert) :: Insert system clipboard register
Ctrl+W (Insert) :: Delete previous word
Ctrl+U (Insert) :: Delete input back to line start
Ctrl+O (Insert) :: Execute one Normal-mode command then resume Insert''')

section('Neovim — search, buffers, splits, tabs and diagnostics')
keys('''/text / ?text :: Search forward / backward; Enter confirms
n / N :: Next / previous search match
* / # :: Search word under cursor forward / backward
:noh :: Clear search highlighting
:%s/old/new/g :: Replace all matches in file
:%s/old/new/gc :: Replace all with confirmation
:s/old/new/g :: Replace matches on current line
:vimgrep /pattern/gj **/* :: Search project files into quickfix (can be slow in large trees)
:copen / :cclose :: Open / close quickfix list
:cnext / :cprevious :: Next / previous quickfix entry
:ls / :buffers :: List buffers
:b name / :buffer N :: Switch to buffer by name / number
:bnext / :bprevious :: Next / previous buffer
:bdelete :: Close buffer; unsaved changes require save or explicit !
Ctrl+^ :: Alternate buffer
:split file / :vsplit file :: Horizontal / vertical split
Ctrl+W then h/j/k/l :: Focus split left/down/up/right
Ctrl+W then w :: Cycle windows
Ctrl+W then c / o :: Close split / keep only current split
Ctrl+W then = :: Equalize split sizes
Ctrl+W then + / - / > / < :: Adjust split height / width
:tabnew file :: Create Neovim tab page
gt / gT :: Next / previous Neovim tab
:tabclose :: Close current tab page
gf :: Open file under cursor (overridden on Markdown links)
:find filename :: Find file using configured path
:terminal :: Open terminal in current window
Ctrl+backslash then Ctrl+N (Terminal) :: Leave terminal input mode
i (terminal buffer Normal mode) :: Re-enter terminal input
:help topic :: Open local Neovim help
Ctrl+] / Ctrl+T (help) :: Follow help tag / jump back
:map / :nmap / :imap :: List effective mappings
:verbose nmap KEY :: Show mapping definition and originating config
:checkhealth :: Check installed runtime and integrations''')

